## How to use

There is a number of stored procedures that can be used for creating log entries in the tables dbo.Log and dbo.LogDetail.

When used from other databases, these procedures and the log and logDetail tables should be represented by synonyms. This is done already for DSA and DataArea modules if they are based on the [templates](https://dev.azure.com/kmd-dima/KMD.DIMA.KIP/_wiki/wikis/KMD.DIMA.KIP.wiki?wikiVersion=GBwikiMaster&pagePath=/Datawarehousing/Platform%20Components/Templates).



```
-- Called to create a log entry in status "Started" and receive an Audit_ID
procedure [dbo].[StartLog](
            @Project nvarchar(50),                  -- the name of the module
            @PackageName nvarchar(50),              -- the name of the subpart of the module
            @TaskName nvarchar(250),                -- the specific table or file being handled
            @SourceSystem nvarchar(50),             -- the source system if applicable
		  @ParentAudit_ID	 int = 0,   -- if this is a nested log, then the parent Audit_ID.
	       @Msg nvarchar(max) = '' ,  -- a text if applicable
		  @DSADataFrom datetime = null,  -- the date that data is from if known
            @Audit_ID int output) -- returns an Audit_ID used in subsequent calls to the log
```


```
-- Called to end a log entry with status "Ok"
    procedure [dbo].[EndLogOK](
                @Audit_ID int,                           -- the audit_id from StartLog
                @Changes int,                            -- the total rows / lines processed
    			@Msg as nvarchar(max) = '')  -- optional message
```

```
-- Called to end a log entry with status "Ok", but delete it if no log entries exist with this as parent.
    procedure [dbo].[EndLogOKDeleteIfNoChildren](
                @Audit_ID int,                      -- the audit_id from StartLog
                @Changes int)                       -- the total rows / lines processed
```

```
-- Called to end a log entry with status "Error"
    procedure [dbo].[EndLogError](
                @Audit_ID int,                          -- the audit_id from StartLog
                @Message nvarchar(max))                 -- optional message
```

```
-- Called when more detailed logging is needed beneath the standard log entries.
    procedure [dbo].[StartLogDetail](
                @MasterAudit_ID int,                    -- the integer obtained from StartLog
                @DetailTaskName nvarchar(250) = '',     -- short text
                @LogLevel nvarchar(20) = '', 	    -- log level (Warning, Error)
    	        @Msg nvarchar(max) = '' ,           -- longer message		  
                @DetailAudit_ID int output)             -- returns an id to use with EndLogDetailOK/Error
```

```
procedure [dbo].[EndLogDetailOK](
                @Audit_ID int,                          -- the DetailAudit_ID obtained from StartLogDetail
                @Changes int = 0,                       -- number of rows / lines changed in total if applicable.
    		  @Inserted int = 0,                -- number of rows / lines inserted if applicable. 
    		  @Updated int = 0,                 -- number of rows / lines updated if applicable.
    		  @Deleted int = 0,                 -- number of rows / lines deleted if applicable.
    		  @Msg as nvarchar(max) = '')       -- detailed info message
```

```
procedure [dbo].[EndLogDetailError](
                @Audit_ID int,             -- the DetailAudit_ID obtained from StartLogDetail
                @Message nvarchar(max))    -- the error message (as human readable as possible)
```
